<span id="A2.T14.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T14.1.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">In a screenplay:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T14.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T14.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A2.T14.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T14.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T14.1.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">- Dialogue includes plot, character speech, actions during speech, emotional states, internal thoughts, character interactions, and psychological elements</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T14.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T14.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A2.T14.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T14.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T14.1.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">- Scene description includes setting details, environment, atmosphere, physical space, sensory elements, and visual imagery without character interactions</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T14.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T14.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="A2.T14.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T14.1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T14.1.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Based on these definitions, classify the following suggestion as either ’dialogue’ or ’scene_description’.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T14.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T14.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
